# Keeps `docker compose build` fast, especially when the Docker daemon is remote (e.g.
# `docker context` over SSH to a real Linux host - see README.md / TODO.md #3): the whole
# build context gets tar'd up and sent to the daemon on every build, and only
# tools/latency_oneway/ and docker/latency-tool/entrypoint.sh are actually needed by
# docker/latency-tool/Dockerfile (both COPY'd via explicit paths, unaffected by this file).
results/
scripts/
.claude/
*.md
